/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Cryptocurrency transactions are recorded on public blockchains, making transaction information available for analysis; however, the pseudonymous nature and complex flow of digital assets can make the investigation of fraudulent and illicit transactions difficult.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
78 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E ( This project proposes an Explainable Graph-Based Cryptocurrency Fraud Investigation Framework for detecting suspicious Bitcoin transactions and analyzing their associated money-flow patterns. The proposed system uses the publicly available Ethereum Dataset, where transactions are represented as nodes and transaction relationships are represented as directed edges. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
